WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:13.400
Tika knows her material. But she walks in looking at the floor, and her hands will not stay still.

2
00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:21.500
The audience reads your body before it hears your words. If the two disagree, the body wins.

3
00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:24.800
Presentation style has three elements.

4
00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:28.100
Physical presence: what they see.

5
00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:32.600
Vocal emphasis: what they hear under the words.

6
00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:39.100
And emotional connection: what they feel when you read the room and respond.

7
00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:48.100
Presence is prepared, not performed. Before she walks in next time, Tika does three things. Feet flat on the floor.

8
00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:52.200
Three slow breaths, longer out than in.

9
00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:59.900
And a home for her hands, so no part of her mind has to watch them.

10
00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:06.000
All of it before she walks in, like an athlete warming up.

11
00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:13.700
The same elements change with the room. One to one: stillness, eye contact, a slower pace.

12
00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:20.200
A small meeting: sit forward, and use your voice to mark the answer.

13
00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:25.500
A large room: wider gestures, a slower pace, real pauses.

14
00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:32.800
A video call: the camera flattens you, so look at the lens and add energy.

15
00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:40.500
The next presentation has the same material. This time her body says what her words say.

16
00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:46.600
She did not copy anyone. She adjusted the elements, not her personality.

17
00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:49.600
The body speaks first.

18
00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:52.900
Presence is prepared, not performed.

19
00:01:52.900 --> 00:02:01.000
Now it is your turn. Before your next meeting: feet, three breaths, a home for your hands.
